  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Sudan Multi Year Resilience Programme (MYRP) 2024-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MYRP 2023-2025 will provide continuity for the twelve counties supported in the original MYRP in Warrap, Unity, Upper Nile, Jonglei, Eastern Equatoria, and Lakes states including Abyei and Pibor, two administrative areas that have been particularly hard hit by crisis in recent years. MYRP focuses on improvement of holistic learning outcomes through ensuring learning is accessible to all girls and boys including those living with disabilities; supporting and monitoring improved academic and skill-based outcomes; and increasing the availability of mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS), and socioemotional learning (SEL).</narrative>
  </description>
